# This package has no `files` field, so npm packs everything not excluded here.
# aai-ui and aai-cli need no equivalent file: both declare `files`, so their
# tarballs already contain only what is listed.

# The committed API Extractor reports (`pnpm api-report`) — a repo artifact for
# reviewing signature changes, not something a consumer installs.
etc/

# Coverage output. This one was SHIPPING: `pnpm check:local` runs
# `test:coverage`, which writes `packages/aai/coverage/`, and any pack after that
# carried 175 HTML and JSON files into the tarball — +900 kB packed, +5.7 MB
# unpacked, on every release cut from a machine that had run the checks first.
# Found by `scripts/artifact-size-report.mjs` on its first real run, which is
# what that report is for.
coverage/

# Turbo's per-package cache metadata. Not ours, never useful to a consumer, and
# present only because a build ran before the pack.
.turbo/
